{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"luminous-stenchful-cottontail","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\nADR 0098 defines one immutable non-secret `OperationSnapshot` per operation. Today CLI and shared command-write entry points still call `emit_shadow_snapshot()`, while store/config helpers can resolve ambient state independently. The reconciler runtime already demonstrates snapshot-derived bindings; reuse that pattern.\n\nThis story cuts ordinary CLI, MCP/Python command, and store-opening operations over. LLM-specific resolution is the dependent follow-up.\n\n## Work\n\n- Census the command/store consumers and identify the public composition boundaries for CLI, MCP, and Python.\n- Compose exactly once after input parsing and before lock/network/write, then pass focused immutable projections/context through shared command/store seams.\n- Preserve explicit-input > environment > project > user > schema precedence and independent repository-root selection from ADR 0098.\n- Add consumer-level metamorphic and effect-spy tests.\n- Remove migrated shadow calls and ambient reloads; extend the existing ownership checker with red-proven detections rather than a second registry.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Representative CLI, MCP, and Python ticket/store reads and writes each compose one snapshot/context, proven by call-count tests through production entry points.\n- [ ] Given environment/config/CWD mutation after composition, the active operation's selected tracker directory, branch, remote, push mode, and observable effects remain unchanged; a new operation observes the change.\n- [ ] Explicit operation input remains authoritative and malformed selected config fails before lock, subprocess, network, or store write.\n- [ ] Store helpers receive focused projections/context and do not call `load_config`, environment, or CWD beneath the approved boundary.\n- [ ] Migrated `emit_shadow_snapshot` calls and compatibility resolution branches are deleted, with no stored ticket/event/bridge format change.\n- [ ] The structural ownership checker catches a synthetic below-boundary ambient read and has zero new legacy exceptions.\n- [ ] Existing config, tracker layout, concurrency, CLI/MCP/library parity, lint, typecheck, and default suites pass.","id":"3a08-4016-0a3a-4be0","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["configuration","store","migration"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Make OperationSnapshot authoritative for CLI, command, and store operations"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788026457668319415,"uuid":"85ec436e-a1b6-457e-bf11-094ebd7c582a"}